# Sensitive tax data — never commit
taxpayer_profile.json
tax_law_*.json
result.json
answers.md
summaries/
documents/*
!documents/.gitkeep
FBAR_*.md
*.pdf
projections/
withholding/
projection_inputs.json
scenarios/
reviews/
# Year-end cutover moves documents/ and reviews/ BENEATH archive/{year}/,
# where the root-scoped rules above no longer reach them.
archive/
holdings.json
parse_ledger.json
crypto_transactions.json
tax_calendar_*.ics
# The PDF generator is written per workspace by tax-generate, so it is a
# runtime artifact despite being source code — and it is the one runtime file
# whose contents the PII gate cannot vet. That gate matches SSN and credential
# SHAPES plus sensitive filenames; a taxpayer's NAME has neither, and a
# generator that hardcodes one in a section header commits cleanly.
generate_tax_pdf.py

# Agent session state — handoffs and plans quote whatever was being worked on.
.planning/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Virtual environment
.venv/

# Environment files (may contain API keys)
.env
.env.*
.env.local

# Editor swap/backup files (may contain partial copies of sensitive data)
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.tmp

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE files
# Exclude .vscode CONTENTS rather than the directory: git never descends into an
# excluded directory, so a negation under `.vscode/` would silently do nothing.
# settings.json is checked in — it is what makes Copilot find .agents/skills.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/

# Hookify local rules (machine-specific, not for sharing). They are generated
# from conversation analysis, so a rule quotes whatever was being worked on when
# it was created — the same disclosure shape as .planning/, not merely a
# preference file.
.claude/*.local.md

# Per-machine Claude Code state. `.claude/settings.json` IS tracked — it carries
# the project's PostToolUse hooks — and `.claude/skills/` holds the tracked
# relative symlinks that give Claude Code project-local discovery. That is what
# makes `.claude/` a directory people `git add`, and equally what rules out
# ignoring the directory itself: git never descends into an excluded directory,
# so a bare `.claude/` line would make the repository's own config and skill
# links uncommittable. Every rule below therefore names an artifact.
#   settings.local.json accumulates per-machine allow rules and absolute paths,
#     and in this clone it grants `Bash(git push:*)`. It was previously covered
#     only by a contributor's own global gitignore, which protects nobody else.
#   .perms-stamp is rewritten by the permissions hook on every tool call.
#   .skill-invariants-stamp is the same for the skill-invariants hook.
#   .archive-dirs is the owner-only directory index used to notice detached
#     writes beneath an existing archived year without walking every file.
#   .archive-files is the owner-only file index used to verify archived file
#     modes without recursively rediscovering the full history on every call.
#   .archive-index-dirty exists only between the two renames that publish those
#     two indexes. Its PRESENCE is what forces a rebuild after a pass dies
#     mid-publish; that job briefly belonged to the absence of .perms-stamp,
#     which conflated it with the incremental boundary of every other tree.
#
# All five end in `*`, for two different reasons. The four data files are never
# written in place: each is built as a `mktemp` sibling (`.perms-stamp.XXXXXX`)
# and moved over the real name, so the settings.json hook timeout firing
# mid-refresh — the routine outcome on a large archive — leaves the sibling
# behind holding exactly the contents the finished file would have had. Under
# the exact-name form that leftover was untracked rather than ignored, which is
# one `git add .` away from committing a NUL-separated index of every archived
# taxpayer document path. The glob covers both the file that is rarely lying
# around and the one that is. On the marker, which IS written in place and holds
# nothing, the glob is merely defensive.
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/.perms-stamp*
.claude/.skill-invariants-stamp*
.claude/.archive-dirs*
.claude/.archive-files*
.claude/.archive-index-dirty*
